watch-pin-dead — rowt #s36 (Hong, #s35 option 1): the 2026-10-30 outage, the
pinned server dead.

The router is up (host.pid.self), the system proxy points at it, the machine
has not moved (watch.net holds this sandbox's net id), and the escape selection
is ONE server: state says selected=alpha and the selector agrees. watch.health
seeds a streak of two, so this tick is the third failed tunnel probe: the clash
delay URL has no fixture, the slower confirmation probe fails the same way, and
the connection list is empty (no fresh flow). The captive probe is pointed at
http://127.0.0.1:8099/success, so the network is CLEAR and nothing holds
recovery for the network's sake. Then the one more question: a direct TCP
connect from the NIC to alpha, 203.0.113.10:443, which times out (curl 28 in
the .rc file) — the server itself is dead.

Expected: no reload. The tick writes watch.hold ("<utc stamp><TAB>alpha"),
logs "pinned server alpha is dead: 203.0.113.10:443 does not accept a TCP
connection over en0 (3 consecutive probe failures) — … the watchdog holds
instead of reloading; 'rowt use auto' fails over by itself …" and one audit
line, and the streak reads 3. Before #s36 this exact world ran cmd_reload —
thirteen times in half an hour on the day, each cutting every lane.
